Dear Clay,
 This is an interesting question!
 You could actually break the monotonicity of the functional form by including a quadratic, even if it is not supported by AIC.
 Secondly, you can edit the oSCR.fit function and remove the "log" or "exp" functions where necessary to enforce an identity link, although I imagine your starting values need to be very very good to fit a model with the identity link!

I don't have any other ideas on that....
regards
andy

