Hey Clayton, this is a really interesting topic.  It definitely goes beyond SCR and gets at the limitations of GLMs in general.  I like Andy's suggestion of a quadratic term, which can do some heavy lifting beyond a linear effect.  Ultimately, your concerns are a motivation for basis functions, which could be accommodated in oSCR.

What are your concerns about realism?  The problem with extrapolation is that you don't have evidence to make predictions beyond the covariate space used to fit the models.

