> The difference probably comes from the fact that in the multisession model you assume detection is constant across sessions (years). To recover the single session model result using a multisession model, I’d add a session effect on detection (and perhaps include an interaction). You could also check the single session output and see which parameters look similar across sessions and which don’t – if there are difference in the detection estimates, that’s the variation you are constraining when not including session.
